  CONCLUSION: page.route() interception is sufficient. NO SSR read of
  src/lib/workflow/dynamo-read.ts is on the /workflow render path, so nothing in
  src/ needs to be stubbed, patched or env-gated. Zero source files are modified.

  Two things deliberately NOT stubbed, because they are bundled client-side and are
  part of what we want to exercise for real:
    - src/config/workflows.json  -> workflow-defs.ts:18 imports it, so the
      "dead-code-sweep" def and its Intake/Detect/Sweep/... phase boxes are the
      REAL ones.
    - src/lib/workflow/run-outcome-display.ts -> the module under test.

=== 2.4  What shape must the fixture events have? ===

  /api/workflow/[id]/events maps every DDB row through transform-event.ts with
  { includeEventId: true }; the three orchestrator events are not members of the
  closed WorkflowEvent union and land on the passthrough:

    src/lib/workflow/transform-event.ts:126-127
      default:
        return base({ type: eventType, ...detail, timestamp });

  So the probe serves them pre-transformed: { eventId, type, ...detail, timestamp }
  — i.e. exactly what the board's reducer and describeOrchestratorEvent() receive
  in production.


